.TH SDL_ResumeAudioDevice 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ResumeAudioDevice \- Use this function to unpause audio playback on a specified device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_ResumeAudioDevice(SDL_AudioDeviceID devid);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function unpauses audio processing for a given device that has previously been paused with
.BR SDL_PauseAudioDevice ()\[char46]
Once unpaused, any bound audio streams will begin to progress again, and audio can be generated\[char46]
.PP
Unlike in SDL2, audio devices start in an _unpaused_ state, since an app has to bind a stream before any audio will flow\[char46] Unpausing an unpaused device is a legal no-op\[char46]
.PP
Physical devices can not be paused or unpaused, only logical devices created through
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDevice ()
can be\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I devid
a device opened by
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDevice ()\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_AudioDevicePaused (3),
.BR SDL_PauseAudioDevice (3)
